1.0.0
  - Converted from standalone Functions\Optimize-VMX.ps1 script into a
    Public\/Private\ module layout matching the other modules here.
  - Added SupportsShouldProcess / -WhatIf / -Confirm support around the
    actual file-write action.
  - Adapter "already correct" detection is now anchored to the full line
    (multiline regex) instead of an unanchored substring match, removing
    any theoretical cross-adapter ambiguity (e.g. ethernet1 vs ethernet10).
  - The hardware-pinning rule loop now stops after the first match, so a
    future overlapping pattern cannot queue conflicting virtualHW.version
    changes.
  - Killing a running vmware-vmx process now polls (up to 5s) for the
    process to actually exit instead of a flat 1 second sleep, so file
    locks are more reliably released before files are rewritten.
  - Skipped/aborted (WhatIf) changes are now correctly counted in the
    summary statistics.
  - Added a log message when no .vmx files are found under -Path.
